cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "STOA: reproducibility package for \"Decide on Arrival\""
message: >-
  If you use this artifact, cite the paper. If you use the attainable-ceiling
  diagnostic specifically, §5.2 of the paper is the part to cite; the one-line
  implementation is stoa.sequential.attainable_ceiling.
type: software
authors:
  - name: "STOA Project"
    email: suanlee@semyung.ac.kr
    affiliation: "Semyung University"
repository-code: "https://github.com/suanlab/stoa"
license: Apache-2.0
abstract: >-
  Code, experiment artifacts and measurement protocol for a study of KV-block
  placement on production Mooncake traces. The central finding is about
  evaluation rather than about a policy: split-instant protocols leave almost
  all of a hindsight oracle's advantage unreachable by construction, so a
  policy measured inside one looks flat however well it ranks. Moving the
  decision to each block's arrival recovers the benefit, and what captures it
  is admission timing rather than prediction.

  The package ships the controls as code, not as prose: every number in the
  paper is re-derived from its artifact by scripts/check_paper_numbers.py,
  every artifact is checked against the source that produced it, and the
  defects this work made and caught are catalogued in
  docs/claims_dependency.md.
keywords:
  - agent memory
  - KV cache
  - memory tiering
  - cache replacement
  - evaluation methodology
  - reproducibility
